1
00:00:11,340 --> 00:00:17,540
Aiming for the setting sun
floating on the Nakagawa,

2
00:00:18,060 --> 00:00:24,660
when I kick a pebble, even my shoes fly off.

3
00:00:25,880 --> 00:00:33,020
Will I ever get to save up for it, I wonder?

4
00:00:33,020 --> 00:00:39,120
They laughed that I'm still just a brat.

5
00:00:39,880 --> 00:00:44,220
Even if I try to chase
some energy somewhere,

6
00:00:44,220 --> 00:00:49,280
Katsushika, yawns and all, nothing changes.

7
00:00:49,280 --> 00:00:53,160
The townscape is strangely gentle.

8
00:00:54,660 --> 00:01:01,120
From the pointed hat's water bottle,

9
00:01:01,660 --> 00:01:07,440
the sunset falls into the great sky.

10
00:01:11,180 --> 00:01:15,920
Tomorrow, too,
it ends just like this, doesn't it?

11
00:01:15,920 --> 00:01:19,740
Katsushika, Shibamata, happiness again.

12
00:01:19,740 --> 00:01:22,420
Upon meeting, I realized.

13
00:01:22,420 --> 00:01:24,580
Because I'm such a fool.

14
00:01:29,100 --> 00:01:31,320
Ryo-san's new recruit training.

15
00:01:40,020 --> 00:01:42,820
This is the Kameari Kōen-mae Hashutsujo!

16
00:01:44,560 --> 00:01:45,060
I see.

17
00:01:45,700 --> 00:01:47,120
This is the famous one.

18
00:01:57,120 --> 00:02:00,040
Kameari Kōen-mae Police Box

19
00:02:00,800 --> 00:02:01,220
Is that so?

20
00:02:04,000 --> 00:02:06,960
Police box duty is the
foundation of police work,

21
00:02:06,960 --> 00:02:08,720
and it is an extremely important job.

22
00:02:08,720 --> 00:02:10,320
Crime prevention and

23
00:02:10,320 --> 00:02:11,780
of course, crime prevention

24
00:02:11,780 --> 00:02:15,160
and the arrest rate of criminals
through street questioning during patrols

25
00:02:15,160 --> 00:02:17,100
are higher than expected.

26
00:02:18,380 --> 00:02:22,040
Police Academy Encyclopedia, page 777.

27
00:02:23,360 --> 00:02:26,160
Let me introduce trainee Miyaji.

28
00:02:26,160 --> 00:02:29,200
Nice to meet you.

29
00:02:30,300 --> 00:02:35,720
Miyaji graduated from Tojo University and
entered the police academy with top marks.

30
00:02:35,720 --> 00:02:39,060
He's an outstanding trainee, personally
endorsed by the university president.

31
00:02:39,060 --> 00:02:39,740
Wow.

32
00:02:40,400 --> 00:02:43,220
Tojo University is a prestigious school,
isn't it?

33
00:02:43,220 --> 00:02:45,840
Yes, he's a future leadership candidate.

34
00:02:47,100 --> 00:02:55,960
Miyaji-kun, if there's anything you don't understand, don't hesitate to ask me.
There's nothing I don't understand, and even if there were, I wouldn't ask you, would I?

35
00:02:55,960 --> 00:02:56,340
Mm.

36
00:02:58,200 --> 00:03:05,380
Please go easy on us, Miyaji-kun. The two over there
are Nakagawa-kun and Akimoto-kun. Nice to meet you.

37
00:03:06,460 --> 00:03:10,000
It's an honor to have an
outstanding trainee like you.

38
00:03:12,900 --> 00:03:16,160
Police Academy Encyclopedia, page 124.

39
00:03:16,160 --> 00:03:18,720
Under the section on the mandatory
wearing of police uniforms.

40
00:03:18,720 --> 00:03:23,020
Clothing other than the regulation uniform is supposed to be prohibited,
Nakagawa-san.

41
00:03:25,120 --> 00:03:27,460
I do have permission, though.

42
00:03:27,460 --> 00:03:30,440
It would be boring if everyone wore the same uniform,
wouldn't it?

43
00:03:34,940 --> 00:03:37,400
Twenty centimeters above
the knee is too short.

44
00:03:38,300 --> 00:03:40,660
Yellow with pink uniforms is improper.

45
00:03:40,660 --> 00:03:41,840
Chief Ohara.

46
00:03:41,840 --> 00:03:43,320
W-what is it?

47
00:03:43,320 --> 00:03:47,880
Do you know what this police box is
rumored to be at the police academy?

48
00:03:48,360 --> 00:03:48,720
No.

49
00:03:49,180 --> 00:03:52,800
The Kameari Kōen-mae police box is
a burden on the Katsushika station.

50
00:03:54,060 --> 00:03:56,260
A dumping ground for
underachieving officers.

51
00:03:56,260 --> 00:03:56,580
What?

52
00:03:57,680 --> 00:04:00,580
The chief's management
skills are also a problem.

53
00:04:03,200 --> 00:04:05,660
My first step toward
distinguished field experience

54
00:04:07,700 --> 00:04:10,440
is something I can't make sense of at all,
given the intentions of upper management.

55
00:04:13,320 --> 00:04:16,040
I'll draw up the training schedule myself,

56
00:04:16,040 --> 00:04:17,560
so please don't trouble yourself.

57
00:04:21,600 --> 00:04:24,620
Terai-san,
please lend me the patrol area map.

58
00:04:25,580 --> 00:04:26,300
Yes.

59
00:04:30,220 --> 00:04:31,280
I-I'm Terai.

60
00:04:31,820 --> 00:04:32,540
Nice to meet you.

61
00:04:37,400 --> 00:04:40,320
I've landed myself with a
really troublesome trainee.

62
00:04:40,320 --> 00:04:41,980
It's only for today, anyway.

63
00:04:41,980 --> 00:04:44,140
Looks like it's going to be a long day.

64
00:04:44,720 --> 00:04:46,080
Yahoo!

65
00:04:49,300 --> 00:04:50,980
Yeah!

66
00:04:50,980 --> 00:04:52,860
Full speed at a hundred
kilometers an hour, Mornie!

67
00:04:53,320 --> 00:04:55,960
Arriving with a dazzling technique!

68
00:04:57,180 --> 00:04:58,840
Yeah!

69
00:04:59,320 --> 00:05:00,120
Wow!

70
00:05:01,040 --> 00:05:02,100
Good morning!

71
00:05:02,780 --> 00:05:03,660
Ryo-chan

72
00:05:03,660 --> 00:05:05,500
Ugh, I'm in trouble now.

73
00:05:07,400 --> 00:05:08,300
I went and backed into something, you know.

74
00:05:09,140 --> 00:05:11,000
And this is a stolen ride, by the way.

75
00:05:11,500 --> 00:05:13,980
Cornering is my life.

76
00:05:13,980 --> 00:05:17,420
Hey, you've wiped out my important data!

77
00:05:17,420 --> 00:05:20,460
You seem to be wearing the regulation uniform,
at least.

78
00:05:20,460 --> 00:05:22,480
Police Academy Primer, Part One, page 125.

79
00:05:22,480 --> 00:05:24,880
Supplementary item on the
officer uniform requirements.

80
00:05:24,880 --> 00:05:28,980
You're violating the ban on sandals and geta.
Who are you?

81
00:05:28,980 --> 00:05:32,100
Me? I'm Kankichi Ryotsu. Who are you?

82
00:05:32,100 --> 00:05:33,720
Good morning, Ryotsu-kun.

83
00:05:33,720 --> 00:05:35,740
You're in a good mood again this morning,
aren't you?

84
00:05:37,400 --> 00:05:38,200
What a noisy guy.

85
00:05:39,400 --> 00:05:40,800
Trainee Miyaji.

86
00:05:40,800 --> 00:05:41,860
Trainee?

87
00:05:42,880 --> 00:05:43,880
Senior Officer Ryotsu.

88
00:05:43,880 --> 00:05:45,200
I'm appointing you for today

89
00:05:45,200 --> 00:05:47,740
as Miyaji's supervising officer.

90
00:05:49,300 --> 00:05:50,700
Supervising officer?

91
00:05:50,700 --> 00:05:52,560
What exactly am I supposed to do, Chief?

92
00:05:53,100 --> 00:05:55,520
Take Miyaji out on patrol.

93
00:05:55,520 --> 00:05:56,520
Understood, Ryotsu?

94
00:05:56,520 --> 00:05:57,220
Chief

95
00:05:57,220 --> 00:05:59,080
I'm fine on my own.

96
00:05:59,080 --> 00:06:01,120
This is a direct order
from the Chief, Miyaji.

97
00:06:01,960 --> 00:06:03,760
Which page was that regulation on again?

98
00:06:04,940 --> 00:06:06,100
Page 572.

99
00:06:07,400 --> 00:06:10,420
7. Absolute obedience to superiors' orders.

100
00:06:13,280 --> 00:06:17,480
Right, today's the day Virtual
Fantasy X arrives at the arcade.

101
00:06:18,040 --> 00:06:24,500
We can do whatever we want if we just fool the trainee.
Alright, hurry up and follow me!

102
00:06:24,500 --> 00:06:27,720
Four of them. Don't fall behind!

103
00:06:28,780 --> 00:06:36,120
Skateboards aren't on the list of approved police equipment lately.
Hahaha, are you alright, Chief?

104
00:06:37,400 --> 00:06:45,120
Leaving it to Ryotsu, the man of brawn, and Miyaji, the man of brains,
combining such different personalities might produce surprisingly good results.

105
00:06:45,120 --> 00:06:48,780
Chief, you really pulled off getting rid of that nuisance,
didn't you? Yeah.

106
00:06:57,180 --> 00:06:59,340
Ten minutes before the arcade's turnover.

107
00:07:02,120 --> 00:07:06,060
I'm the one who's putting the
first coin into the new game machine.

108
00:07:06,060 --> 00:07:07,020
Ryo-san.

109
00:07:08,280 --> 00:07:11,200
Aren't you off the designated patrol course?

110
00:07:11,200 --> 00:07:12,700
It's fine. This way.

111
00:07:12,700 --> 00:07:15,700
But around Kameari Elementary,
Middle, and High School.

112
00:07:15,700 --> 00:07:19,160
The official course is heading out toward
Katsushika Station from the police box.

113
00:07:20,240 --> 00:07:22,580
What's the point of
touring such boring places?

114
00:07:22,580 --> 00:07:26,480
My patrol is set: arcades,
pachinko, and the model shop.

115
00:07:26,480 --> 00:07:28,520
Then isn't that just
touring amusement arcades?

116
00:07:29,340 --> 00:07:36,580
Please return to the course.
If you don't like it, let's split up. You go that way, I'll go this way. Meet in two hours.

117
00:07:36,580 --> 00:07:43,380
Let's meet back at the police box.
Wait a moment. Page 843, new trainee training, number 20.

118
00:07:43,380 --> 00:07:55,180
Patrol training must always be accompanied by an active-duty officer.
I don't care what you say, you're just playing games. Are you ignoring the Chief's orders and abandoning my supervisory responsibility?

119
00:07:56,140 --> 00:08:00,480
At this rate, Virtual Fantasy X, my main
reason, will be taken by someone else!

120
00:08:01,640 --> 00:08:02,380
Fine.

121
00:08:03,200 --> 00:08:05,580
Alright, we'll take the official course.

122
00:08:11,980 --> 00:08:13,760
I'll shake him off somewhere along the way.

123
00:08:15,300 --> 00:08:17,660
Kameari Elementary School area, no problems.

124
00:08:20,920 --> 00:08:24,680
Hey, do you always carry
something like that around with you?

125
00:08:25,500 --> 00:08:25,970
Yes,

126
00:08:26,020 --> 00:08:30,360
thanks to that, I was always top of my class,
from university through police academy.

127
00:08:30,840 --> 00:08:34,140
But being smart alone won't make
you fit to be a police officer.

128
00:08:34,140 --> 00:08:37,040
If anything, academic credentials
are more of a hindrance.

129
00:08:37,960 --> 00:08:43,940
What a police officer needs is not knowledge but rather adaptability,
sound judgment, and the ability to act.

130
00:08:44,460 --> 00:08:45,600
Adaptability.

131
00:08:45,600 --> 00:08:47,680
Ryo-san!

132
00:08:50,200 --> 00:08:52,100
Where are you going, Ryo-san?

133
00:08:52,680 --> 00:08:54,180
This is what adaptability is.

134
00:09:02,900 --> 00:09:03,660
Finally.

135
00:09:05,720 --> 00:09:06,780
Phone time-wasting!

136
00:09:07,100 --> 00:09:08,640
Three minutes left to go.

137
00:09:08,640 --> 00:09:12,300
If I dash in the moment the arcade shutter opens,
I've got a chance.

138
00:09:17,660 --> 00:09:18,800
Now that's quick.

139
00:09:18,800 --> 00:09:24,300
Alright, I'll suggest to the Chief that
every patrol officer be issued a skateboard.

140
00:09:24,960 --> 00:09:26,880
30 seconds till the spin!

141
00:09:30,840 --> 00:09:31,780
It's open!

142
00:09:32,320 --> 00:09:33,620
I'm so excited!

143
00:09:33,620 --> 00:09:35,760
Virtual Fantasy X

144
00:09:35,760 --> 00:09:37,580
Doggy Go

145
00:09:41,740 --> 00:09:43,400
Yes! I'm the first one here!

146
00:09:44,320 --> 00:09:46,400
So this is Virtual Fantasy X!

147
00:09:48,520 --> 00:09:49,280
Charm period!

148
00:09:50,040 --> 00:09:50,960
W-what made you figure it out?

149
00:09:51,260 --> 00:09:54,240
Judging from your words and actions,
there's no other possibility!

150
00:09:54,520 --> 00:09:56,840
Damn it!

151
00:09:59,900 --> 00:10:02,640
I'm the first one!

152
00:10:05,400 --> 00:10:06,820
Heh, I've got it!

153
00:10:06,820 --> 00:10:21,060
Aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaah...

154
00:10:21,060 --> 00:10:25,340
I broke the solo patrol code rules
right at the start of my training.

155
00:10:25,740 --> 00:10:27,920
Nobody will find out if we
just keep quiet about it.

156
00:10:27,920 --> 00:10:29,820
Is that so?

157
00:10:30,200 --> 00:10:30,820
What should I do?

158
00:10:31,780 --> 00:10:32,500
What should I do?

159
00:10:32,500 --> 00:10:32,720
What should I do?

160
00:10:32,720 --> 00:10:33,340
What should I do?

161
00:10:34,580 --> 00:10:37,600
You ditched me just so you could play that game,
didn't you?

162
00:10:38,820 --> 00:10:42,260
No, of course it's for patrol, obviously.

163
00:10:44,020 --> 00:10:45,800
Police box duty rule number 30.

164
00:10:45,800 --> 00:10:48,560
It's preferable to cover patrol efficiently
and leave the rookies to handle the rest.

165
00:10:48,560 --> 00:10:51,700
If we don't hurry to the next location,
we won't get through everything in time.

166
00:10:52,340 --> 00:10:55,640
Don't be stupid.
A pro goes with his gut and bets on a spot.

167
00:10:55,640 --> 00:10:58,080
Once you've picked a spot,
you stick with it till the end.

168
00:10:58,080 --> 00:11:00,020
That's the secret to patrol.

169
00:11:00,020 --> 00:11:02,000
We're staying here for about an hour.

170
00:11:04,200 --> 00:11:06,940
I've never heard of a patrol
that's basically gambling.

171
00:11:07,320 --> 00:11:07,900
Well then.

172
00:11:07,900 --> 00:11:09,320
Let's go.

173
00:11:11,100 --> 00:11:12,740
Then just one more round of that game.

174
00:11:13,200 --> 00:11:14,160
That's not allowed.

175
00:11:27,060 --> 00:11:29,080
Suspicious vehicle, no persons of interest.

176
00:11:30,140 --> 00:11:30,900
Nothing unusual to report.

177
00:11:31,460 --> 00:11:33,640
Leave something like that
to the traffic division.

178
00:11:35,900 --> 00:11:37,380
From headquarters to all mobile units.

179
00:11:37,720 --> 00:11:39,800
At the arcade in the
station-front shopping street.

180
00:11:40,320 --> 00:11:41,840
We've arrested Marunichi,
the coin-changer thief.

181
00:11:41,840 --> 00:11:42,440
What?

182
00:11:47,940 --> 00:11:49,200
Good work, sir.

183
00:11:57,180 --> 00:11:58,360
The coin-changer thief.

184
00:11:58,360 --> 00:11:59,800
Just as I said.

185
00:11:59,800 --> 00:12:01,640
If we'd just stuck it out right here.

186
00:12:01,640 --> 00:12:03,420
A first catch for a trainee.

187
00:12:03,420 --> 00:12:06,000
Too bad, Miyaji.

188
00:12:06,000 --> 00:12:08,940
Don't tell me you committed this crime...

189
00:12:10,320 --> 00:12:12,230
I sensed it, of course.

190
00:12:12,280 --> 00:12:17,020
As a senior officer, my sense of smell
is keenly attuned to the scent of crime.

191
00:12:17,260 --> 00:12:18,380
The scent of crime?

192
00:12:18,600 --> 00:12:21,240
They closed up. It's coming along. Chance.

193
00:12:22,220 --> 00:12:27,040
Listen, this isn't something you
can pick up just by studying a little.

194
00:12:27,500 --> 00:12:30,140
My sense of smell is tingling again.

195
00:12:30,520 --> 00:12:33,062
This way? This way? This way!

196
00:12:33,112 --> 00:12:34,840
Alright, let's go, Miyaji.

197
00:12:35,620 --> 00:12:36,340
Yes.

198
00:12:40,620 --> 00:12:44,620
Shall we drop in? Right, we're stopping by.

199
00:12:44,620 --> 00:12:47,720
What's in this shop?

200
00:13:04,860 --> 00:13:06,500
Cash is the way to go, after all.

201
00:13:06,500 --> 00:13:09,620
Racking up high scores at the arcade won't fill your belly,
you know.

202
00:13:10,260 --> 00:13:11,840
I've finished patrolling the store.

203
00:13:12,960 --> 00:13:14,200
Next, to Setogi...

204
00:13:14,200 --> 00:13:16,300
Don't tell me you just wanted time to play.

205
00:13:17,720 --> 00:13:21,920
I doubt it. To you, who let a crime that could have
been prevented slip away right under your nose...

206
00:13:21,920 --> 00:13:27,640
You probably can't understand my thinking. Even sitting here like this,
my keen sense of smell is always

207
00:13:27,640 --> 00:13:29,520
picking up on what's happening around us.

208
00:13:35,500 --> 00:13:39,000
Didn't you think that man who
just passed was acting strange?

209
00:13:39,000 --> 00:13:40,060
Miyaji.

210
00:13:40,060 --> 00:13:45,900
Let's take a closer look at that man. Arrest of a
suspect through a routine questioning during patrol.

211
00:14:17,440 --> 00:14:18,380
Stop it!

212
00:14:19,900 --> 00:14:21,060
What the hell are you doing?!

213
00:14:21,380 --> 00:14:24,140
I don't know! I asked what he does for a living,
and suddenly - !

214
00:14:24,180 --> 00:14:25,260
Ow ow ow ow ow

215
00:14:25,260 --> 00:14:26,540
What a pathetic excuse for a trainee!

216
00:14:26,800 --> 00:14:28,420
Didn't you ever practice judo?!

217
00:14:29,020 --> 00:14:30,480
I'm a third-degree black belt, though.

218
00:14:30,480 --> 00:14:35,020
Your third-degree judo can't
even beat a prank that small?!

219
00:14:35,680 --> 00:14:36,380
Hey, old man!

220
00:14:49,180 --> 00:14:50,220
In the moment his hand faltered,

221
00:14:50,220 --> 00:14:51,380
Surrounded by women!

222
00:14:51,900 --> 00:14:52,920
Ear-pulling!

223
00:14:52,920 --> 00:14:53,960
On!

224
00:14:54,960 --> 00:14:56,300
Oh no! Oh no! Oh no!

225
00:14:58,020 --> 00:14:59,980
I'm the very embodiment of adaptability!

226
00:15:02,860 --> 00:15:04,320
Got it, Miyaji?

227
00:15:05,060 --> 00:15:05,860
This is...

228
00:15:06,340 --> 00:15:07,440
it looks like a suicide note.

229
00:15:08,060 --> 00:15:08,600
A suicide note?

230
00:15:09,620 --> 00:15:10,040
What?

231
00:15:11,500 --> 00:15:15,460
I was laid off from the
company I'd worked for 30 years.

232
00:15:17,720 --> 00:15:21,800
I'm sorry I lost my temper earlier.

233
00:15:22,220 --> 00:15:23,300
No harm done.

234
00:15:25,920 --> 00:15:27,620
As long as you're alive,
good things can still happen.

235
00:15:27,620 --> 00:15:28,640
Someday, maybe.

236
00:15:29,400 --> 00:15:29,760
Thank you very much.

237
00:15:32,260 --> 00:15:33,380
Excuse me.

238
00:15:34,800 --> 00:15:35,980
Cheer up.

239
00:15:36,600 --> 00:15:39,260
Are we sure it's alright to
just let him go like that?

240
00:15:39,260 --> 00:15:41,120
I was about to strangle you.

241
00:15:41,120 --> 00:15:42,920
As long as he has that kind of energy,
he'll be fine.

242
00:15:43,640 --> 00:15:45,120
In just one hour,

243
00:15:45,120 --> 00:15:46,680
we sensed a crime,

244
00:15:46,680 --> 00:15:48,440
and saved a person's life!

245
00:15:48,940 --> 00:15:49,980
Maybe this guy is

246
00:15:49,980 --> 00:15:52,400
a rare, outstanding police officer.

247
00:15:53,880 --> 00:15:55,780
By the way, what exactly is
"restructuring" anyway?

248
00:15:56,200 --> 00:15:57,560
Is it some rare creature?

249
00:15:58,180 --> 00:15:59,500
Nope, never mind.

250
00:16:01,000 --> 00:16:03,020
All that exercise made me hungry.

251
00:16:08,680 --> 00:16:11,460
The dango here is delicious
no matter when you eat it.

252
00:16:11,460 --> 00:16:14,720
Sorry, Ryo-san,
for asking you something like this.

253
00:16:15,200 --> 00:16:15,580
Thanks.

254
00:16:16,960 --> 00:16:19,680
Still, it's lucky we happened to pass by.

255
00:16:19,680 --> 00:16:22,820
Right. If it had rained,
it would have turned into a flood.

256
00:16:22,820 --> 00:16:23,940
Yoisho.

257
00:16:25,360 --> 00:16:28,440
What do you mean by
"happened to"? You came here just to eat dango.

258
00:16:28,880 --> 00:16:31,640
That's part of the job too,
so do it properly.

259
00:16:31,640 --> 00:16:32,340
Phew.

260
00:16:32,340 --> 00:16:32,924
What,

261
00:16:32,974 --> 00:16:36,780
has there been even one mistake
in anything I've said so far?

262
00:16:37,260 --> 00:16:41,160
You're stubborn, and you lack
hands-on experience by a wide margin.

263
00:16:41,600 --> 00:16:43,740
That's why working three times as hard
as everyone else is just right for you.

264
00:16:43,740 --> 00:16:44,620
Phew.

265
00:16:46,140 --> 00:16:47,320
Well, do your best.

266
00:16:47,320 --> 00:16:47,960
Eei!

267
00:16:47,960 --> 00:16:48,860
Eei!

268
00:16:53,860 --> 00:16:55,400
See, you can do it if you try.

269
00:16:56,020 --> 00:16:57,320
I can't move anymore.

270
00:16:57,320 --> 00:16:59,320
Well, well, thank you very much.

271
00:16:59,320 --> 00:17:01,840
Ryo-san, this is a bathhouse ticket.

272
00:17:01,840 --> 00:17:03,200
Would you like to use it?

273
00:17:03,200 --> 00:17:04,480
Miyaji.

274
00:17:04,480 --> 00:17:07,980
Looks like the warm kindness of the
residents has come back to us right away!

275
00:17:08,560 --> 00:17:11,340
Is it really alright for public
servants to accept something like that?

276
00:17:11,340 --> 00:17:14,640
We mustn't waste people's
kind consideration.

277
00:17:14,640 --> 00:17:17,060
Let's adapt and go to the bathhouse.

278
00:17:21,900 --> 00:17:29,100
Nice! Is it really all right to take a bath while on duty?
What's the big deal? You got filthy cleaning the gutter too.

279
00:17:29,100 --> 00:17:36,200
Wouldn't you feel gross staying like that? That's true,
but we've already washed it off, so let's hurry back to patrol.

280
00:17:36,200 --> 00:17:40,160
Fine, fine. But first...

281
00:17:40,160 --> 00:17:44,820
Wash my back, pleeeease!
Blizzard body, 300 pages.

282
00:17:45,180 --> 00:17:47,420
Absolute obedience to superiors' orders.

283
00:17:47,420 --> 00:17:49,520
It's page 572.

284
00:17:49,520 --> 00:17:50,260
I see.

285
00:17:54,920 --> 00:17:56,140
That feels refreshing.

286
00:17:56,140 --> 00:17:59,920
Look, it's not like you just have
to cover the official patrol route.

287
00:18:00,380 --> 00:18:02,960
I may look like I'm just
goofing off at first glance, but

288
00:18:02,960 --> 00:18:05,500
I'm still doing good
for the residents, right?

289
00:18:06,220 --> 00:18:08,760
So that's why you go to arcades
and pachinko parlors during work?

290
00:18:08,760 --> 00:18:12,780
That's right. It's so I can see
the world from all kinds of angles.

291
00:18:12,780 --> 00:18:18,120
*Thud* Is that a scale?
Let's see how much it weighs.

292
00:18:18,760 --> 00:18:26,260
Is that a model kit? You can't build that here,
you'll get in people's way. Sorry!

293
00:18:27,640 --> 00:18:29,540
Once it's finished,
let's go show it off before we leave.

294
00:18:30,900 --> 00:18:34,880
Let's see, *oof*... What's this?

295
00:18:34,880 --> 00:18:35,660
Oh no, this is... what do I do?

296
00:18:35,940 --> 00:18:38,340
It's glue! Who the hell left this here!

297
00:18:40,280 --> 00:18:41,260
It won't come off!

298
00:18:41,660 --> 00:18:42,840
It's instant glue!

299
00:18:44,240 --> 00:18:45,240
Do something!

300
00:18:47,260 --> 00:18:48,200
What are you doing?

301
00:18:48,560 --> 00:18:51,060
It's a piggyback!
We have to get back on patrol quickly!

302
00:18:55,800 --> 00:18:56,520
What's wrong?

303
00:18:56,800 --> 00:18:59,040
My knees have stuck together too!

304
00:18:59,280 --> 00:18:59,640
What?

305
00:19:06,620 --> 00:19:09,340
Aaaaaah

306
00:19:09,340 --> 00:19:12,980
Aaaaaah

307
00:19:12,980 --> 00:19:14,060
Aaaaaah

308
00:19:14,060 --> 00:19:15,080
Aaaaaah

309
00:19:15,080 --> 00:19:17,880
Aaaaaah

310
00:19:17,880 --> 00:19:17,920
Aaaaaah

311
00:19:34,260 --> 00:19:35,760
We're going way too fast!

312
00:19:36,380 --> 00:19:36,940
Whoa!

313
00:19:37,880 --> 00:19:38,900
Aaaaaah!

314
00:19:39,700 --> 00:19:40,600
What was that!

315
00:19:40,900 --> 00:19:43,680
I'm so embarrassed I could die.

316
00:19:43,680 --> 00:19:45,520
Aaaaaah!

317
00:19:46,220 --> 00:19:48,120
An intersection! We're gonna hit a car!

318
00:19:48,320 --> 00:19:49,480
I don't want to die!

319
00:19:49,840 --> 00:19:51,120
Okay! Change direction!

320
00:19:51,180 --> 00:19:52,260
How?

321
00:19:52,700 --> 00:19:55,180
Hang on! Shift your weight into the turn!

322
00:19:55,560 --> 00:19:56,460
Nngh! Nngh!

323
00:19:57,940 --> 00:20:00,620
Hey! You wiggle your butt too!
Do you want to die?

324
00:20:01,560 --> 00:20:02,900
Let's do it again! Ready?

325
00:20:05,400 --> 00:20:07,200
Shake! Go for it!

326
00:20:08,200 --> 00:20:08,940
Do it!

327
00:20:09,440 --> 00:20:11,020
Look! It's just like a skateboard!

328
00:20:11,820 --> 00:20:14,400
Yes! One of my hobbies came in handy again!

329
00:20:14,640 --> 00:20:15,960
Alright! Behind us!

330
00:20:16,080 --> 00:20:18,760
Crap! It's a church!

331
00:20:19,220 --> 00:20:20,940
Now then, the exchange of rings.

332
00:20:23,440 --> 00:20:25,800
Yes! Number three! Right!

333
00:20:26,180 --> 00:20:26,520
Yes!

334
00:20:27,780 --> 00:20:28,840
Congratulations!

335
00:20:30,900 --> 00:20:33,560
Coming down the aisle in that state...

336
00:20:37,380 --> 00:20:38,440
Aaaaaaah!

337
00:20:39,640 --> 00:20:41,700
We did it!
We're out on the national highway!

338
00:20:42,160 --> 00:20:43,220
Finally stopped.

339
00:20:44,160 --> 00:20:46,500
Isn't this embarrassing,
out here in the middle of town?

340
00:20:47,120 --> 00:20:48,140
It can't be helped!

341
00:20:48,320 --> 00:20:50,480
Since neither of us can get our legs off.

342
00:20:57,640 --> 00:20:58,660
Intersection!

343
00:20:59,560 --> 00:21:00,320
Truck!

344
00:21:02,000 --> 00:21:03,040
It's an intersection!

345
00:21:03,560 --> 00:21:04,880
You're making fools of us!

346
00:21:04,880 --> 00:21:06,580
Look, Miyaji, it's a chase!

347
00:21:07,040 --> 00:21:08,680
I can't do it with this bicycle!

348
00:21:08,900 --> 00:21:13,360
Idiot! If we let him get away here, we'll
waste a huge amount of manpower and taxes!

349
00:21:14,880 --> 00:21:17,540
That's why our initial actions
as field officers are crucial!

350
00:21:19,580 --> 00:21:20,220
Understood!

351
00:21:20,700 --> 00:21:21,400
Alright, let's go!

352
00:21:23,200 --> 00:21:26,120
Got it! The car!

353
00:21:27,940 --> 00:21:29,940
Hey! Who are you!

354
00:21:30,140 --> 00:21:31,600
Chase the bike I just mentioned!

355
00:21:31,860 --> 00:21:32,440
Yaaah!

356
00:21:44,300 --> 00:21:44,860
The suspect went

357
00:21:48,620 --> 00:21:49,600
and turned left.

358
00:21:49,600 --> 00:21:51,200
Right, change course!

359
00:21:51,200 --> 00:21:52,180
Gonna shake off the glue!

360
00:21:52,180 --> 00:21:54,620
Ready, set, three!

361
00:21:56,520 --> 00:21:58,500
Oops, we shook too hard!

362
00:21:58,500 --> 00:21:59,720
Ryo-san, the car!

363
00:22:00,680 --> 00:22:04,020
Young man, I may be naked right now,
but I'm still a cop!

364
00:22:04,020 --> 00:22:06,040
Sorry, but please follow
the motorbike ahead.

365
00:22:06,040 --> 00:22:09,180
You're Ryo-san from the Kameari Park police box,
aren't you?

366
00:22:10,020 --> 00:22:11,340
Alright, leave it to me.

367
00:22:11,740 --> 00:22:13,300
Thank you for your cooperation.

368
00:22:18,780 --> 00:22:19,560
Alright, let's go!

369
00:22:19,560 --> 00:22:22,240
The road ahead is closed for construction.

370
00:22:22,240 --> 00:22:23,020
Ryo-san!

371
00:22:23,020 --> 00:22:23,400
Yeah.

372
00:22:24,380 --> 00:22:26,180
I think my legs are about to come off!

373
00:22:26,180 --> 00:22:26,740
What?

374
00:22:30,840 --> 00:22:31,460
They're coming back!

375
00:22:31,460 --> 00:22:32,680
He's coming this way!

376
00:22:39,500 --> 00:22:43,700
Nice work!

377
00:22:45,400 --> 00:22:46,200
Where's Ryo-san?

378
00:22:51,140 --> 00:22:55,160
The man ran out of the bank
onto the street at 3-chome,

379
00:22:55,160 --> 00:22:57,600
Wow, even after getting into that state,

380
00:22:57,600 --> 00:23:00,320
you managed to corner the
suspect with quick thinking.

381
00:23:00,320 --> 00:23:01,800
Great job, Miyaji!

382
00:23:01,800 --> 00:23:04,800
Oi! Oi!

383
00:23:05,920 --> 00:23:07,080
Senpai?

384
00:23:07,560 --> 00:23:09,920
What on earth are you doing in that state?

385
00:23:12,040 --> 00:23:13,600
What happened to the bank?

386
00:23:14,300 --> 00:23:16,680
Miyaji-kun brilliantly subdued him,
you know.

387
00:23:16,680 --> 00:23:18,860
Looks like the Chief's Award is a sure thing,
you know.

388
00:23:19,340 --> 00:23:20,900
What? The Chief's Award?

389
00:23:21,360 --> 00:23:22,037
Miyaji,

390
00:23:22,087 --> 00:23:25,480
Our cut is you and me, the shibaroku split.

391
00:23:26,020 --> 00:23:29,800
Idiot! You don't get a cut!

392
00:23:29,960 --> 00:23:33,540
What! I helped Miyaji
with the bank robbers too!

393
00:23:33,540 --> 00:23:37,420
Reports came in of a naked
editor riding a bicycle,

394
00:23:37,840 --> 00:23:39,440
flooding Katsushika Station.

395
00:23:40,100 --> 00:23:41,980
Today it's only a reprimand report, Man-san!

396
00:23:42,220 --> 00:23:43,100
It's a bulletin!

397
00:23:44,660 --> 00:23:47,200
Miyaji was shaking his butt naked too,
wasn't he?

398
00:23:47,200 --> 00:23:52,040
Ryo-chan, at times like this,
your everyday reputation is what counts.

399
00:23:52,040 --> 00:23:54,320
That's right, senior.

400
00:23:54,320 --> 00:24:00,980
How cruel! This manuscript deadline is awful,
so heartless, heartless, heartless!

401
00:24:04,860 --> 00:24:07,060
To save a toy factory
on the verge of collapse,

402
00:24:07,060 --> 00:24:11,220
the figure I made has forty points of articulation.
It's an amazing piece!

403
00:24:12,420 --> 00:24:15,480
Alright, I'll sell, sell,
sell like crazy and make a fortune!

404
00:24:15,480 --> 00:24:16,960
Everyone, you'd better buy them too!

405
00:24:17,980 --> 00:24:21,260
Look forward to the next
mass-produced doll release, okay?

406
00:25:27,020 --> 00:25:34,420
Thanks for watching.

